WEBVTT

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:44.370
O-Otose!

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.590
Why are you here?!

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:47.590
Madame Otose...

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:51.380
Stop this silly fighting.

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:54.600
Let's make peace and 
celebrate at my bar.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:56.100
H-Huh?!

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:58.260
Pirako, you're coming too.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:00.710
Since you made a real mess of things

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:04.220
you'll have to make up for it
with one hell of a show.

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:06.150
Otose...

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:08.150
Whatcha babbling about, old lady?

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:10.850
We don't have time for that!

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:14.040
Finish up your business then.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:15.910
How long are you guys going to lie there?

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:19.280
This old lady came out here

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:21.410
despite being seriously injured.

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:24.060
Enough of your petty bickering.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:28.420
There's a serious fight in the 
works, with Edo on the line.

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:33.020
If you don't protect 
this town, who will?

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:35.020
We may be moving in 
different directions,

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:36.930
but we all started in the same place.

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:40.430
The yakuza, trannies, cabaret girls...

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:44.190
We all love this town.

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:49.180
That's all there is to it.

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:52.950
Otose-san! Look out!

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:57.010
Hey, if you wanna snuff

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:59.660
one of the Four Devas while I'm around,

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:01.910
come back in a hundred years!

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:04.420
B-Bro!

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:06.820
What are you fools doing?!

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:09.800
You always return the 
favor, seven for three!

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:11.550
Well, Gran?

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:15.220
Show them our...

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:19.220
No, show them the Kabuki 
District's might.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:25.560
<b>'Tis An Honor!</b>

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.400
Wh-Who's there?

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:33.900
A bandit who's opened 
the door to paradise...

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:35.420
Catherine the lock picker!

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:36.910
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:40.910
Why did you shut the door 
without saying anything?!

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:43.660
Do you realize how hard it 
was for me to get here?!

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:45.650
They found me!

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:47.010
Hey! Open the door!

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:48.220
Help!

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:49.420
Stay away!

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:50.400
Don't come any closer!

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:54.630
Wh-Who's there?

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:58.640
You scared him because of your 
funny clothes, Catherine.

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:00.140
That's right.

00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:02.500
Don't worry!

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:06.140
The Kabuki Cats are here now!

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.200
B-Bro!

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:14.190
What are you fools doing?!

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:17.650
You're gonna stand around while 
the Amanto take over our town?!

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:20.160
Ka-Katsuo...

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:23.720
Young lady, we were the 
castoffs of society

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:26.180
until the boss took us in.

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:29.720
We're prepared to throw away

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:34.170
our worthless lives for the 
boss, and for his daughter.

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:35.570
However...

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:38.700
We aren't gonna abandon 
the town our boss

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:40.700
has dedicated his life to protecting.

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:44.680
We have a duty to protect 
the Kabuki District!

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:46.930
Take a good, hard look!

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:50.190
This is the town your old 
man has been protecting!

00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:51.440
Let's do this!

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:56.110
The whole universe will learn 
to fear the Jirocho Gang!

00:04:57.010 --> 00:05:00.700
The Kabuki District belongs to us!

00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:02.270
Heh...

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:07.300
They're the ones who made 
a mess of this town.

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:10.210
That's why I can't stand yakuza.

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:18.880
The Kabuki District belongs to you?

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:22.500
No.

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:24.890
It belongs to us trannies!

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:29.440
It's finally time for us to go crazy!

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:32.400
Show them the true power of a tranny!

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:38.150
Loud and clear, everyone.

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:43.320
This is the Kabuki District!

00:06:41.690 --> 00:06:44.150
Fr-Freaks...

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:49.260
Kill them in the name of the Harusame!

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:35.230
Finish them!

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:39.240
Pops,

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:41.710
we promise to protect everything

00:07:41.710 --> 00:07:43.570
which was dear to you.

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:45.110
Jirocho...

00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:51.080
Take care of her... Take 
care of our town...

00:08:08.510 --> 00:08:09.510
They did it!

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:12.510
There were only two of them.

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:17.520
My elite soldiers lost 
to these base monkeys.

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:20.760
This can't be... This can't be...

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:27.570
That's...

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:29.260
Otose!

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:40.080
I never expected this filthy 
town to be home to such heroes.

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:42.590
Mark my words, Jirocho...

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:47.090
The Harusame will return this favor!

00:08:48.990 --> 00:08:50.720
W-Wait...

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:03.800
All this effort to chase 
a vixen out of town.

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:05.730
I don't want to get any older.

00:09:06.530 --> 00:09:11.010
But you young'ns are disappointing.

00:09:13.180 --> 00:09:15.560
When I was a young lad...

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:17.380
The elderly always let nostalgia

00:09:17.380 --> 00:09:19.370
cloud their memory.

00:09:19.630 --> 00:09:21.970
I don't want to get any older.

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:24.540
Hey, kid.

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:26.880
Is that his jutte?

00:09:27.890 --> 00:09:30.060
Why do you have it?

00:09:31.490 --> 00:09:35.140
I made a one-sided promise, 
and then I swiped it.

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:36.140
Heh.

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:40.200
Same here.

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:47.150
Whenever I smoke, the 
memories come back.

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:50.280
I would watch from behind

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:53.080
as he walked around, toying with his jutte

00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:55.120
while smoking with his left.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:58.020
It was rather striking to see him

00:09:58.020 --> 00:10:00.080
with the Kabuki District as a backdrop.

00:10:00.520 --> 00:10:03.180
He loved this town,

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:06.670
and I'm sure that this town loved him.

00:10:06.670 --> 00:10:11.410
We can smoke and fiddle with a jutte,

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:14.180
but we can never be like him?

00:10:14.410 --> 00:10:17.840
He died the way he lived.

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:19.730
Like a man,

00:10:19.730 --> 00:10:22.550
who sacrificed his life 
for someone like me

00:10:22.550 --> 00:10:24.150
while leaving loved ones behind.

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:27.190
I killed him.

00:10:28.970 --> 00:10:33.570
So I had to give up on being 
a man, on being human,

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:37.160
in order to protect what he left behind.

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:40.900
Even if the town hated me for it...

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:42.210
Damn...

00:10:42.580 --> 00:10:45.060
So you weren't trying to kill Gran.

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:50.210
She's always been a pain in the ass.

00:10:50.510 --> 00:10:54.220
Squawking in my ear whenever 
I did something...

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:58.890
My resolve would waver when I saw her.

00:10:59.410 --> 00:11:00.900
When I watched you guys,

00:11:00.900 --> 00:11:05.520
I would get the urge to go 
back to being the old Jirocho.

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:09.560
You're getting in my way, Tatsugoro.

00:11:11.550 --> 00:11:14.240
Let's settle this once and for all.

00:11:14.950 --> 00:11:19.740
We'll see who's worthy of 
inheriting his pipe and jutte.

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:22.620
I'm not interested in any inheritances.

00:11:22.940 --> 00:11:25.750
I just wanted to keep 
my promise this time.

00:11:26.890 --> 00:11:31.750
It's obvious that neither of 
us is going to cave or give in.

00:11:32.140 --> 00:11:33.640
In that case...

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:36.650
...there's only one way 
for us to move forward.

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:45.120
I will keep my promise and survive.

00:11:45.490 --> 00:11:46.480
In return...

00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:49.190
...you will keep your promise...

00:11:49.860 --> 00:11:51.440
...and die.

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:55.260
Both of you are chained to 
this town by the same thing.

00:11:55.740 --> 00:11:59.660
A promise made to a certain man.

00:12:00.550 --> 00:12:03.450
An iron vow of your own choosing.

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:06.220
The chains of a warrior.

00:12:08.670 --> 00:12:10.670
Old man!

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:27.970
Your promise was broken.

00:12:28.340 --> 00:12:29.690
I win.

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:36.700
Bastard...

00:12:37.530 --> 00:12:39.450
Why didn't you cut me down?

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:41.450
Like I said...

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:45.450
I'm going to keep my promise this time.

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:46.790
Pops,

00:12:46.790 --> 00:12:48.520
we promise to protect

00:12:48.520 --> 00:12:50.580
everything which was dear to you.

00:12:53.070 --> 00:12:55.430
Quit smoking, old timer.

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:10.350
I'd appreciate it if you 
never woke up again.

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:12.770
Usually, you wouldn't put 
a guy in the same room

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:14.110
as the person he stabbed.

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:17.820
This can't be a hospital.

00:13:18.140 --> 00:13:19.760
Must be some kind of haunted house.

00:13:20.300 --> 00:13:21.370
What was that, Seirogan?!

00:13:21.960 --> 00:13:26.870
Looks like everyone managed 
to survive somehow.

00:13:27.220 --> 00:13:28.980
Had nothing to do with us.

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:30.870
Our lives were saved.

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:32.820
Your daughter spent

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:35.920
three days taking care 
of you without any sleep.

00:13:36.380 --> 00:13:39.630
And your daughter kept an eye on me

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:43.140
to make sure I didn't run off 
again and exacerbate my injuries.

00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:45.820
A futile effort.

00:13:45.820 --> 00:13:48.190
We can stab you, tie you up,

00:13:48.190 --> 00:13:49.460
and you'll still get back up.

00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:52.150
You're one to talk, stubborn mule.

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:55.590
I know that I'm stubborn,

00:13:55.590 --> 00:14:01.010
but you make me look like 
a reasonable fellow.

00:14:01.010 --> 00:14:06.160
Everybody turned out to 
be as twisted as he was.

00:14:06.810 --> 00:14:10.650
Actually, you're worse 
than Tatsugoro was,

00:14:10.650 --> 00:14:13.820
since you beat me in a battle of wills.

00:14:13.820 --> 00:14:17.130
You look pretty happy for 
someone who was beaten.

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:19.170
Yeah...

00:14:19.740 --> 00:14:22.560
It's been so long since 
I've had a real fight.

00:14:23.180 --> 00:14:27.180
A real fight between men and warriors.

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:31.190
I can only laugh after losing 
in such a satisfying way.

00:14:31.190 --> 00:14:35.390
I've given up so much to be 
able to keep my promise...

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:40.740
But he managed to save everything 
to keep his promise,

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:41.780
including me.

00:14:42.810 --> 00:14:45.910
No, I was just running away...

00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:48.790
I was scared of losing 
anyone else dear again...

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:54.790
He shattered the ungainly 
chains around my neck.

00:14:54.790 --> 00:14:59.800
They made it clear that they could 
protect this town without me.

00:15:01.260 --> 00:15:03.000
Twenty years...

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:05.520
I spend twenty years keeping my promise,

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:07.450
and this is how it ends.

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:09.390
In the end,

00:15:09.390 --> 00:15:12.000
I just made everyone around me unhappy,

00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:14.810
while failing to keep my promise.

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:17.320
Otose...

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:21.320
You've done a lot for me.

00:15:21.610 --> 00:15:25.330
But I kept running in circles.

00:15:25.330 --> 00:15:29.330
I was never able to return the favor.

00:15:30.390 --> 00:15:34.830
Sorry I couldn't make you happy.

00:15:35.860 --> 00:15:38.360
Jirocho, I'm...

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:43.840
Damn! What are people doing?!

00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:46.300
It was about to get good!

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:48.680
I told you to stop pushing!

00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:51.440
It's your fault for bringing 
such a big camera!

00:15:51.440 --> 00:15:52.170
Shut up!

00:15:52.170 --> 00:15:54.460
How often are we gonna get to see 
the boss in a romantic scene?!

00:15:54.460 --> 00:15:55.570
Men are so hopeless.

00:15:55.570 --> 00:15:57.630
The sensitivity of a brick.

00:15:57.630 --> 00:15:59.020
What's that in your hand?!

00:15:59.440 --> 00:16:01.210
Please stop this, everyone.

00:16:01.210 --> 00:16:02.110
Recording mode off.

00:16:02.110 --> 00:16:03.470
I just heard something!

00:16:03.470 --> 00:16:04.640
You were recording!

00:16:04.640 --> 00:16:05.700
You were recording the entire time!

00:16:05.700 --> 00:16:08.080
What are you people doing here so late?!

00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:09.760
Wait, that's alcohol!

00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:11.000
Don't you realize what 
kind of place this is?!

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:13.310
This is ours!

00:16:13.310 --> 00:16:15.660
Do you realize how much 
effort it took to get

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:17.710
the old lady on top of the roof?!

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:19.590
Jirocho...

00:16:19.590 --> 00:16:23.210
You and Gintoki will never change.

00:16:23.430 --> 00:16:26.840
You're both selfish jerks.

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:30.710
The difference is that he had 
people to help him realize

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:36.770
that other people needed 
him the way he needed them.

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:42.370
Now, you can see that 
there's no need to worry.

00:16:42.370 --> 00:16:45.290
There are plenty of fools 
in the Kabuki District

00:16:45.290 --> 00:16:47.740
to carry on the spirit 
of you and Tatsugoro.

00:16:48.310 --> 00:16:50.720
You did a fine job of 
protecting this town

00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:53.180
until the next generation 
could take over.

00:16:53.180 --> 00:16:55.220
You kept your promise.

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:58.750
So you can let go now.

00:16:59.210 --> 00:17:05.340
You have other promises to keep.

00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:10.590
I'm very happy right now, Jirocho.

00:17:11.300 --> 00:17:14.310
I met Tatsugoro here 
in the Kabuki District.

00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:16.810
And I met them.

00:17:17.310 --> 00:17:21.860
And I met our beloved Jirocho again.

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:30.890
Thanks for everything, Jirocho.

00:17:35.040 --> 00:17:36.580
This isn't good.

00:17:36.580 --> 00:17:39.190
My eyesight's starting to fail me.

00:17:39.790 --> 00:17:42.920
First, I can't control my bowels,

00:17:42.920 --> 00:17:45.340
now I'm leaking up here.

00:17:45.340 --> 00:17:49.340
<b>Greater Edo Hospital</b>

00:17:46.740 --> 00:17:49.340
I don't want to get any older.

00:17:50.910 --> 00:17:53.010
We cannot allow them 
to get away with this.

00:17:53.390 --> 00:17:55.260
Just you wait, Devas.

00:17:55.550 --> 00:17:57.940
I can no longer turn back.

00:17:57.940 --> 00:17:59.980
I will do anything to obtain 
the Kabuki District.

00:18:00.790 --> 00:18:02.980
I've been waiting for you, Lady Kada.

00:18:04.050 --> 00:18:04.980
You're...!

00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:08.490
Sorry, but could you not interfere?

00:18:08.500 --> 00:18:12.490
I finally get to see my old man look...

00:18:12.490 --> 00:18:13.980
Silence!

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:16.990
Don't you understand that you're 
the one who's interfering?!

00:18:17.410 --> 00:18:19.000
I do.

00:18:19.220 --> 00:18:21.000
My interference is over.

00:18:21.440 --> 00:18:24.540
But I'm taking you with me!

00:18:24.750 --> 00:18:27.550
You're the only one who's leaving!

00:18:29.970 --> 00:18:32.050
Br-Bro!

00:18:32.050 --> 00:18:33.640
Sacrificing yourself 
to take out the enemy...

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:35.690
won't be enough to make up

00:18:35.690 --> 00:18:37.560
for everything you've done, bitch!

00:18:37.990 --> 00:18:39.520
There you have it.

00:18:39.990 --> 00:18:42.060
Whatcha gonna do now, Pirako-chan?

00:18:43.240 --> 00:18:45.840
My job is finished.

00:18:45.840 --> 00:18:48.570
You can have your way with me.

00:18:48.790 --> 00:18:50.460
Sad.

00:18:50.460 --> 00:18:53.570
Don't you need to settle 
things with your old man?

00:18:54.030 --> 00:18:55.830
I have.

00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:59.080
You took all the glory though.

00:18:59.670 --> 00:19:02.140
You're the one who saved my old man.

00:19:02.140 --> 00:19:04.580
I didn't expect you to protect him...

00:19:04.880 --> 00:19:07.040
No, it wasn't just you.

00:19:07.610 --> 00:19:09.250
This town has

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:12.530
wonderful people who help one another

00:19:12.530 --> 00:19:14.140
despite their differences.

00:19:14.140 --> 00:19:16.090
They do more than take away...

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:18.710
If I could be like them...

00:19:20.870 --> 00:19:22.960
But it's okay now.

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:25.000
The father I wanted to see...

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:27.860
The father who Mom and I were waiting for...

00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:31.490
...is back.

00:19:33.240 --> 00:19:35.560
Bro... Everyone...

00:19:35.560 --> 00:19:38.170
I can't apologize for what I've done,

00:19:38.170 --> 00:19:40.380
but let me say this.

00:19:41.280 --> 00:19:43.780
Thank you for letting me see my

00:19:43.780 --> 00:19:45.620
father one last time!

00:19:46.090 --> 00:19:50.330
I couldn't be my father's 
daughter or the Bro's underling,

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:54.580
but I was very happy to be 
a resident of this town,

00:19:54.580 --> 00:19:56.060
if only for a moment.

00:19:56.570 --> 00:19:58.670
Please let me take responsibility 
for what I've done...

00:19:59.410 --> 00:20:01.430
Sorry, but I'm not 
sadistic enough to beat

00:20:01.430 --> 00:20:03.280
up a crying little girl.

00:20:03.280 --> 00:20:04.690
Besides, I'm tired.

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:07.110
Go wait at the place listed there.

00:20:07.590 --> 00:20:10.440
I'll deal with you once I'm healed up.

00:20:10.710 --> 00:20:12.820
You better be done crying by then.

00:20:16.950 --> 00:20:19.160
Let's try that place next time.

00:20:19.160 --> 00:20:19.950
Sure.

00:20:19.950 --> 00:20:23.950
<b>Bar Chono</b>

00:20:20.340 --> 00:20:21.400
What?

00:20:21.400 --> 00:20:23.950
You want to know who the strongest 
man in the Kabuki District is?

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:26.630
You must be new in town.

00:20:26.630 --> 00:20:29.710
Won't last long with that attitude.

00:20:30.230 --> 00:20:31.590
Forget it.

00:20:31.590 --> 00:20:33.210
This town is on a whole different level.

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:34.210
It's too dangerous.

00:20:34.740 --> 00:20:37.070
With the fall of the Deva Kada

00:20:37.070 --> 00:20:38.830
and the retirement of the Deva Jirocho,

00:20:38.830 --> 00:20:43.210
the fragile balance of power 
is beginning to crumble.

00:20:43.680 --> 00:20:46.970
The town's never been this tense before.

00:21:34.490 --> 00:21:36.780
Is that you, Bro?

00:21:37.740 --> 00:21:39.030
'Tis an honor.

00:21:39.420 --> 00:21:42.760
I was born and raised in 
the Kabuki District of Edo,

00:21:42.760 --> 00:21:46.150
where I lived as a ruffian 
in a town of ruffians,

00:21:46.150 --> 00:21:50.290
always surrounded by steel.

00:21:50.290 --> 00:21:54.820
I am ashamed to admit 
that I have walked astray

00:21:54.820 --> 00:21:57.380
and was guided by my brothers

00:21:57.380 --> 00:21:59.080
to embark on a journey of redemption

00:21:59.080 --> 00:22:01.350
to regain that which I have lost.

00:22:02.640 --> 00:22:07.840
I have been called boss, 
warrior, and many other names,

00:22:07.840 --> 00:22:09.850
but I have given them up.

00:22:11.710 --> 00:22:14.060
I am the father of Pirako Chin,

00:22:14.060 --> 00:22:17.680
Jirocho.

00:22:19.650 --> 00:22:22.280
It's rude, but may I ask who you are?

00:22:22.900 --> 00:22:28.090
I-I am the newest member 
of the Odd Jobs family

00:22:28.090 --> 00:22:30.490
in the Kabuki District of Edo...

00:22:30.490 --> 00:22:33.830
On a journey to find my missing father...

00:22:35.530 --> 00:22:41.780
I was guided here by the 
kindness of my brothers.

00:22:43.150 --> 00:22:45.300
I am the daughter of Jirocho,

00:22:45.300 --> 00:22:48.030
Pirako Chin!

00:22:52.040 --> 00:22:55.480
We must have been brought 
together by fate.

00:22:55.480 --> 00:22:57.110
Would you mind

00:22:58.350 --> 00:23:01.610
if I accompanied you on your journey?

00:23:36.980 --> 00:23:38.600
I'm home.

00:23:40.110 --> 00:23:45.070
<b>Next Episode: Odd or Even</b>

00:23:41.160 --> 00:23:42.460
Next time:

00:23:42.460 --> 00:23:43.520
Odd

00:23:43.520 --> 00:23:45.070
Or even?
